 religion here is to  begin with immediate  immediate meaning unmediated right or  mittelbach so  we have to sketch out the mediations and  as a matter of fact this is a little bit  of a digression but  when hegel talks about something being  immediate  by now you know okay there's always more  to the story so there's there's really  two sides to this that work together  part of it is uncovering the structures  where there is mediation going on where  something is not so  cut and dried as it appears at the  beginning but like i said there's more  to the story there's other things  happening and now we make those evident  the other thing is sometimes we  introduce mediation as well so as the  phenomenologist we can be witnessing  mediation we can also be as the  phenomenologist watching the agency  seeing somebody introduce  mediation and these play off of each  other and so this is going to be quite  quite important  you

